  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` conflicts with ARCH-4.\n\n`OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repos, and I can't see their code from here. ARCH-4 only allows additive changes to the event. Renames and removals have to go through deprecation. If either consumer still reads `channel`, dropping it would break a deployed service. \"Nothing reads it\" may be true inside this repo (`src/core/events.ts:16` and `:50` are the only producers), but this repo can't confirm it for the consumers.\n\nHere are the options:\n\n1. **Deprecate in the event, remove from the model (my suggestion).**\n   - I drop `channel` from the `Order` model, `NewOrder`, validation and the `CHANNELS` list.\n   - I keep `channel` on `OrderPlaced` but mark it `@deprecated`.\n   - Because the model no longer has the value, the event would emit a fixed placeholder (e.g. `\"unknown\"`).\n   - That placeholder is itself a behaviour change for consumers. If they branch on `channel`, I'd rather keep the real value until you've confirmed they don't.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this if you can confirm that billing-service and analytics-ingest don't read `channel`, or that Architecture has signed off on the removal. I'd then remove it from the event, the model, request parsing, validation and the tests, and update the docs examples in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n3. **Deprecate only.** I mark the field deprecated in the event and the model with no behaviour change, and you remove it after the consumers have migrated.\n\nThere's one more effect to decide on. `POST /orders` currently rejects an invalid or missing `channel` with 400. After removal, the API would either ignore the field or stop validating it, so existing clients that still send it keep working.\n\nWhich option do you want? If it's option 2, please confirm the consumers have been checked.",
